WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.500
FormalSLT.
Learning guarantees that survive adaptation.

00:04.500 --> 00:07.450
The next observation can depend
on everything seen so far.

00:07.450 --> 00:09.600
Model selection and repeated looks matter.

00:09.600 --> 00:13.350
In one refresh family,
4,608 coordinates reduce to one hit rate.

00:13.350 --> 00:16.050
A hit records the known deterministic step.

00:16.050 --> 00:20.300
Hit-rate differences equal row TV.
Assumes the family; does not test membership.

00:20.300 --> 00:25.400
Four mechanisms: exponential processes,
PAC-Bayes, every time, dependent paths.

00:25.400 --> 00:27.550
Each result is pinned to its Lean source.

00:27.550 --> 00:34.040
One event stays valid at every time
for every allowed posterior.

00:34.040 --> 00:39.790
Choose posterior and tilt from the past.
Fix the score before the next state.

00:39.790 --> 00:45.690
For finite-state kernels, a Poisson correction
connects one path to stationary risk.

00:45.690 --> 00:51.140
Four layers: PAC-Bayes, sequential inference,
dynamics, and VC theory.

00:51.140 --> 00:54.890
Exact Lean receipt:
forward empirical-Bernstein catalog event.

00:54.890 --> 00:57.790
Exact Lean receipt:
refresh-model row-TV identity.

00:57.790 --> 01:00.890
No project-specific axioms.
Pinned revision shown.

01:00.890 --> 01:04.228
FormalSLT.
Checked learning theory for data that adapt.
